  "id": "ENT054",
  "title": "The Five-Block Balance",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "mechanical puzzles",
  "premise": "A maker must place blocks of weights 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 on a toy balance while leaving exactly one block unused. They set 1+5 opposite 2+4, leaving 3 as the prize pedestal; both sides total 6 and the final block displays the answer.",
  "hook": "Use four blocks. Leave one out. Make it level.",
  "visible_action": "Numbered blocks move between pans; totals appear; 1 and 5 settle opposite 2 and 4; unused 3 rises as a pedestal.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Equal totals can come from different combinations.",
  "gate": "Verified 1+5=2+4=6 with one unused block. Present this as one valid solution, not the only solution; ideal equal-arm balance model.",
